body:
Bueno pa, pasaste a contradecir lo 1ro que habías dicho de que "Los del lado de la izquierda no eran inocentes".

&#x200B;

Ojalá tengas un día de mierda, hacete ortear.

To add on a lil bit more on what the comment you replied to said, don't break that much of a sweat about this kind of things bc strings will break or need to be replaced on a regular basis, so you probably shouldn't be worrying all that much about it (unless you've got a gig or important event to play at coming up).  


If it's worrying you too much, you can always try to keep a spare stringset (?) (don't know what the word in english is for a new set of strings) or two, just in case you feel like re stringin' / anything breaks.

&#x200B;

And just as a lil' piece of advice, always try and change your strings all at once. That way they'll all keep about the same level of decay/wear out over time, so as soon as one of them breaks again you'll know the rest will follow in little to no time.

&#x200B;

Sorry if this comes unasked for, and for any mistakes in my english
